  The new catch-all SPA handler concatenates untrusted URL path segments directly into filesystem paths (`public_dir / full_path` and later `dist_dir / full_path`) and serves them when `is_file()` is true. A request such as `/../../../.git/config` can escape the intended payload/build trees and read files outside `/v2/frontend/public` and `/v2/frontend/dist` (e.g., repo metadata/other project files), which is a directory-traversal read exposure on a public endpoint. This can be fixed by resolving the candidate path and enforcing a strict prefix check against the mount root before serving.
