## 3. Root cause

The `v2_production_payload_freshness_refresher.py` `TARGETS` tuple covers only five descriptor families:

| TARGETS entry | `loop_module` |
|---|---|
| `v2_native_ingestors` | `v2_native_ingestors_live_loop` |
| `v2_feature_pipeline_native_snapshot` | `v2_feature_pipeline_native_loop` |
| `v2_rl_core` | `v2_rl_core_inference_loop` |
| `v2_orchestrator_arbitration` | `v2_orchestrator_arbitration_loop` |
| `v2_trade_management_paper` | `v2_trade_management_paper_loop` |

The three stale per-source descriptors (`v2_market_ingestor`, `v2_kucoin_ingestor`, `v2_liquidation_ingestor`) are absent from this list. There is no `v2_market_ingestor_live_loop`, `v2_kucoin_ingestor_live_loop`, or `v2_liquidation_ingestor_live_loop` module. The descriptors are produced only by one-shot CLI invocations and therefore decay past the 900s threshold within ~15 min of the last invocation.

## 4. Why no remediation was performed

CLAUDE.md *Evidence Integrity Rule* forbids producing summaries that are presented as evidence. A "remediation" that rewrites `generated_utc`/`last_run_ts` on these three descriptors would:

1. Produce a timestamp that does not correspond to any underlying producer activity (summary-not-evidence).
2. Be silently re-staled by every subsequent freshness check, because the refresher TARGETS still won't touch them.
3. Risk falsely satisfying downstream gates (public payload freshness guard, codex governor) and unblocking flows that depend on a live producer being present.

